<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.3" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[; ColorBar: A color bar plot for NetLogo
;
; Version: 1.0.0
; Author: Daniel Vartanian
; Maintainer: Daniel Vartanian <https://github.com/danielvartan>
; License: GPLv3 <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0>
; Repository: <https://github.com/danielvartan/colorbar>
;
; Require: NetLogo >= 7.0.0

to plot-color-bar [#plot-name]
  set-current-plot #plot-name
  clear-plot
  set-plot-x-range 0 1
  set-plot-y-range 0 1

  let #pen (range 1 11)
  let #pen-length length #pen
  let #pen-interval 1 / #pen-length
  let #pen-color n-values #pen-length [random-float 100]

  let #pen-range map [
    #i -> (list ((#i - 1) / #pen-length) (#i / #pen-length))
  ] #pen

  let #line-step-size 0.01
  let #line-step 0

  (foreach #pen #pen-color #pen-range [
    [#i #j #k] ->
      create-temporary-plot-pen (word #i)
      set-plot-pen-interval #pen-interval
      set-plot-pen-color #j

      while [#line-step < 1] [
        plotxy (first #k) #line-step
        plotxy (last #k) #line-step

        set #line-step #line-step + #line-step-size
      ]

      set #line-step 0
  ])
end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="295" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-16" height="39" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="1.061" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="39" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="16" updateMode="0" maxPxcor="16" minPxcor="-16"></view>
    <plot x="10" autoPlotX="false" yMax="1.0" autoPlotY="false" y="55" xMin="0.0" height="120" legend="false" xMax="1.0" yMin="0.0" width="325" display="Color Bar">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
    </plot>
    <button x="10" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="280" display="Plot Color Bar">plot-color-bar "Color Bar"</button>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[# COLORBAR

## WHAT IS IT?

`ColorBar` is a [NetLogo](https://www.netlogo.org) model demonstrating how to create a simple color bar plot. Since NetLogo does not include a built-in color bar widget, this model provides a workaround by drawing one using temporary plot pens.

![NetLogo Web Badge](netlogo-web-badge)

Click [here](https://danielvartan.github.io/colorbar/) to see this model online on [NetLogo Web](https://www.netlogoweb.org)!

A [NetLogo extension](https://github.com/NetLogo/NetLogo/issues/2559#issuecomment-3334999283) may be developed in the future to simplify color bar creation. For now, this model serves as a practical example.

For another color bar implementation in NetLogo, see the [`LogoClim`](https://github.com/sustentarea/logoclim) model.

## HOW IT WORKS

The color bar can be drawn in any plot using the `plot-color-bar` procedure (see it in the *Code* tab). This procedure takes the plot name as an argument and creates a random color bar with 10 different colors. The implementation can be adapted to fulfill specific requirements.

## HOW TO USE IT

Click on the *Plot Color Bar* button to visualize the color bar. No setup is required.

This model was developed using NetLogo 7.0.3, so it is recommended to use this version or later.

## HOW TO CONTRIBUTE

![Contributor Covenant 3.0 Badge](contributor-covenant-3-0-badge)

Contributions are always welcome! Whether you want to report bugs, suggest new features, or help improve the code or documentation, your input makes a difference.

Before opening a new issue, please check the [issues tab](https://github.com/danielvartan/colorbar/issues) to see if your topic has already been reported.

